# Documentation (Envy)

- One canonical doc per topic; search `docs/` and extend an existing doc
  before creating one. New primary entry points go in
  `docs/00_index/CURSOR_INDEX.md` and `docs/00_index/README.md`.
- Layout: `docs/00_index/` index and decisions, `docs/10_dev/` build and
  workflow, `docs/20_arch/` architecture, `docs/30_protocols/<proto>/`
  protocol notes, `docs/40_quality/` security/testing, `docs/50_user/` user
  guides. Keep the small pointer files (`docs/STATUS.md`, ...) aligned.
- Developer docs start with `Status`, `Last updated`, `Scope` and
  `Source of truth` lines; update `Last updated` on substantive edits.
- Link claims to code paths, specs or fixtures. English, short sections,
  plain Markdown.
